From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sound Tester <soundtester@invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs42xx8: defer the probe while the codec is held in
 reset

The Audio Injector Octo's machine driver pulses the CS42448's reset line in
its own probe: low, high, low, high, 500 ms each. The codec is a separate
I2C device that probes on its own schedule, and when that lands inside the
pulse the chip does not acknowledge its address: "failed to get device ID,
ret = -121". cs42xx8 then fails for good, and the card defers forever
waiting for a codec that will never register -- no sound card at all.

Which of the two probes first is down to module load order. It had been
winning by luck; with the Bluetooth stack loading alongside (hci_uart,
btbcm, bluetooth) it lost on every boot tried, and a manual rebind of the
codec brought the card straight back.

Treat a bus error reading the chip ID as "not ready yet" and defer. The
deferred probe runs again once another driver binds, by which time the
pulse is over; a codec that is genuinely absent stays deferred and quiet.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [works around the out-of-tree Octo driver]
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42xx8.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42xx8.c
@@ -590,6 +590,13 @@
 	ret = regmap_read(cs42xx8->regmap, CS42XX8_CHIPID, &val);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to get device ID, ret = %d", ret);
+		/*
+		 * A codec that does not answer on the bus may only be held in
+		 * reset by its machine driver for the moment: try again later
+		 * rather than give up on it for good.
+		 */
+		if (ret == -EREMOTEIO || ret == -ENXIO || ret == -EIO)
+			ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
 		goto err_enable;
 	}
 
